 @CorporateShill66  lol, there's no actual distance of object in rendering. the game engine calculate the object distance, simulating light, reflection, etc. then the gpu render the frame. The rendered frame is like a 2D picture. The distance that you see is simulated by your brain.
What makes difference is how well the game do the calculation of whats going on in the scene. Thats why you get more frames when looking straight up to the sky.
Doom can have a lot going on while maintain high framerate, it is superior in calculation, therefore optimization.

